Hi Stain,

In the mirt package code (see line 125-127 at https://github.com/philchalmers/mirt/blob/master/R/M2.R), a high-dimensional IRT model appears to correspond to any model that has more than 3 factors and is not a multiple-groups model (I think that's what 'discrete' stands for in the code below).

Best,
Will

